[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65594,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipoma is a benign tumour of mature adipocytes.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65595,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8850/0 Lipoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65596,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E80.0 &amp; XH1PL8 Lipoma &amp; Lipoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65597,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> conventional or classic lipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65598,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65599,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These most commonly occur in the vulva but may occur in any location.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65600,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipoma presents as a superficial, solitary, soft, mobile, and painless mass {24946809; 24629715; 19853747}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65601,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas occur in adults of reproductive age, as well as in children {24946809; 24629715; 19853747}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65602,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65603,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>An abnormal karyotype is present in the majority of conventional lipomas. The most common alteration involves 12q13-q15, resulting in fusion of <em>HMGA2</em> with a variety of gene partners {9530339}. Other reported chromosomal abnormalities include 6p and 13q rearrangements {9530339}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65604,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas are lobulated, well circumscribed, and sometimes covered by a thin membrane. The cut surface is homogeneously yellow, with thin fibrous septa dividing the tumour into lobules. Focal haemorrhage can be present {19853747}. Tumours have been reported to exceed 15&nbsp;cm in greatest dimension {24629715}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65605,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours consist of a relatively uniform population of mature adipocytes arranged in sheets and/or separated into lobules by thin fibrous septa {24946809; 24629715; 19853747}. Adipocytes and septal stromal cells lack cytological atypia; lipoblasts are not present. Degenerative changes, including myxoid stromal change and fat necrosis, can occur, particularly in larger tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65606,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65607,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In larger tumours, lack of <em>MDM2</em> amplification may be helpful to exclude atypical lipomatous tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65608,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> superficial location; uniformly sized mature adipocytes; lack of atypical stromal cells in fibrous septa.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> in large tumours (&gt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;cm), lack of MDM2 or CDK4 expression by immunohistochemistry or absence of <em>MDM2</em> amplification.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65609,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65610,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign tumours.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:18:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]